# Claude Code hook config + agent instruction file (local-only)
.openclaude/
CLAUDE.md
CODEBASE_REVIEW.md

# Agent scratch space + task briefs (local-only, never commit)
# BRIEF*.md are working documents for a single task; .hermes/ and
# plans/ are the agent's own run state. None of it belongs in history:
# they churn per session, and plans/ can contain transcripts or paths
# that are not meant to be shared. This file is the whole enforcement --
# the repo ships no pre-commit hook, see "Git guardrails" in README.md.
# It only covers the default add, so `git add -f` or a tool that stages
# paths directly still gets them in: read `git status` before committing.
.hermes/
plans/
BRIEF*.md

# Log files (audit, scraper, hook) — could contain user URLs and job content
*.log
*.log.*
logs/
log/

# Backup folders — encrypted data + key + audit trail; never commit
flow_job_backups/
flow_job_backup_*/

# Encrypted store artifacts (in case anyone symlinks userData into the repo
# or copies a file out for debugging; safe defaults)
apply-assistant-data.json
apply-assistant-data.json.*
apply-assistant-key
apply-assistant-key.wrapped
kdf.json
manifest.json
manifest.hmac
